  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b0e1-da5b-fffc-763b" name="Normans (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>NORMAN ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.38-39), from the rise of armoured cavalry under Charlemagne to the Third Crusade.
Characters: the army must have a General (not enforced) and may have an Army Standard Bearer. Cavalry at least a quarter of the points; Infantry up to half; Special Troops, Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to a quarter, with one artillery piece per 500 points.
Ferocious Charge: if a unit noted as having a ferocious charge charges and wins the round of combat, its opponent automatically breaks with no Leadership test. Enemy units that normally ignore Break tests roll a D6: on 1-3 they are broken anyway, on 4-6 they hold.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Special Troops, Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
